    "who": {"x": -760, "y": 0, "w": 600, "fill": "blue", "size": "m", "text": "v4: the wiki comes first\n\nMost visits are someone looking something up. So the default screen is the wiki: search, pages, and how much to trust each section.\n\n• Readers (everyone): Home, Search, Page, Trust actions, You.\n• Anyone can suggest an edit from a page.\n• Page authors and reviewers also see a Workspace link in the top bar. The review tools live there, out of readers' way.\n• Owner: Operations and Settings inside Workspace."},
    "labels": {"x": -760, "y": 760, "w": 600, "fill": "gray", "size": "m", "text": "Trust labels, everywhere content appears\n\nSame icon + words on Home, Search results, the page table of contents, section headers and links.\n\n● Checked against source (a person checked this version)\n◐ Reviewed (approved, not source-checked)\n○ Not reviewed\n▲ Under re-check (report confirmed, retracted source…)\n⬣ Confirmed error\n\nPage label = its worst section, with the spread shown next to it."},
    "reader": {"x": -760, "y": 1750, "w": 600, "fill": "green", "size": "m", "text": "What readers can do about trust\n\n1. See why: every label opens its evidence.\n2. I checked a source: records a source check on this exact version.\n3. I used it in practice: what for, did it work.\n4. Report a problem: wrong, outdated, unclear, bad source.\n5. Follow: hear when a section you used changes or goes under re-check.\n\nCounts stay hidden until you act; readers see team counts, never names."}
